From 2bd6d982edcf9f9bbaa5b413d8c679daeac5fc24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristian <kristian@apache.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:36:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Reject schema registry store passwords without a store

The schema registry client fails to start when it is given a key store or
trust store password without the store's location, with an error that
names the client's own property, and ignores a key password without a key
store. Reject these combinations when the configuration is validated, and
test that the connector starts with the registry properties, rejects a
missing trust store file and a key store password without a key store.
Also cover missing store files and passwords that contain a colon.
